# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: princ-without-argument-returns-nil -- (princ) should return the null symbol, so the REPL echo is blank
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: divergence
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-03

* Observed

#+begin_example
_$ (princ)
nil
_$ (type (princ))
nil
#+end_example

On AutoCAD and BricsCAD (princ) with no argument returns the NULL SYMBOL --
a symbol whose print name is empty: (type (princ)) is SYM and the console
echoes nothing. That is the reason every AutoLISP command function ends in
(princ): "exit quietly". clautolisp returns nil, so the REPL prints nil.

Found while implementing spec 5.6 rule 3 for the cadtui console (alref
Phase 4 S3): a CAD command line runs as (progn (command ...) (princ)) so
that, as at the vendors' prompt, nothing is echoed -- and clautolisp
echoes nil.

* To do

Make PRINC / PRIN1 / PRINT with no argument return the null symbol
(and check that the value printer prints it as nothing, that (null (princ))
is NIL, and that no test relies on nil). The spec's PRINC entry should say
so if it does not; verify against the vendor pages before changing it.
Probe-confirmable: (vl-symbol-name (princ)) -> "" on both vendors.
